<section class="text-base-content">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-12 pb-20 md:px-10 md:pt-20 md:pb-28">
    <div class="grid gap-6 border-b border-base-300 pb-10 md:grid-cols-12 md:items-end">
      <div class="md:col-span-8">
        <p class="tag text-primary">The table</p>
        <h1 class="mt-5 text-[clamp(3rem,7vw,7rem)] leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.015em] text-balance">Breakfast on the <em>roof</em></h1>
      </div>
      <p class="text-lg text-base-content/80 md:col-span-4">Every morning from eight to half past ten, included in every stay.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="mt-10">
      <div class="aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-box sm:aspect-[16/9] md:aspect-[21/9]" data-settle data-sun>
        <img src="/media/roof.jpg" class="size-full object-cover">
      </div>
      <figcaption class="script mt-3 text-lg text-base-content/75">The roof at eight, before the sun comes over the hills.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-16">
      <div class="prose-linen text-lg">
        <p>Marisol Cruz cooked for twenty years in her mother's fonda in Tlacolula before she came to us. She goes to the market at seven, and breakfast is whatever looked best there: the fruit, the cheese, the herbs for the eggs.</p>
        <p>The chocolate is ground for us in a mill on Calle Mina, with cinnamon and a little almond, and whisked with water the way it is drunk in the valley. Tell us the night before if you would rather have it with milk.</p>
      </div>
      <blockquote class="border-l-[1.5px] border-dashed border-primary pl-6 text-[clamp(1.75rem,2.6vw,2.4rem)] leading-snug text-balance self-start"><p class="display">“I cook breakfast the way my mother did for people who came a long way to the market: enough to walk on until three.”</p><footer class="tag mt-4 text-base-content/70">Marisol Cruz</footer></blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
